<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="AfterYouveGone-G-Theme" spTempo="164">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1918
Composer:	Turner Layton
Lyricist:	Henry Creamer
Form:	20-bar chorus, A–B–A–C with a 4-bar extension
Key:	Bb major

“After You’ve Gone” is unusual among jazz standards
because its chorus is much shorter than the typical
 32-bar form. It was introduced as a song with both
a verse and chorus, but jazz performances generally
focus on the compact 20-bar chorus.</spComments>
